ANNEX K
(Clause 8.7) VIBRATIONS IN BUILDINGS K-1   GENERAL In order to design the buildings safe against vibrations, it is necessary to identify the source and nature of vibration.
Vibrations may be included in the buildings due to various actions, such as:
a) human induced vibrations, for example, the walking or running or a single person or a number of persons or dancing or motions in stadia or concert halls;
b) machine induced vibrations;
c) wind induced vibrations;
d) blast induced vibrations;
e) traffic load, for example, due to rail, fork-lift, trucks, cars, or heavy vehicles;
f) airborne vibrations;
g) crane operations; and h) other dynamic actions such as wave loads or earthquake actions.
