8.6.2.1 General
Explosions may cause impulsive loading on a structure. The following types of explosions are particularly relevant:
a) Internal gas explosions which may be caused by leakage of gas piping (including piping outside the room), evaporation from volatile liquids or unintentional evaporation from surface material (for example, fire);
b) Internal dust explosions;
c) Boiler failure;
d) External gas cloud explosions; and e) External explosions of high explosives (TNT, dynamite).
The codal requirement regarding internal gas explosions is given in 8.6.2.2.

